{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.not_of_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.not_of_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L163-L177","doc":"**Refuted over a one-point index** — the property the old schema lacked\nentirely.\n\n`local_variation` cannot hold when there is nowhere to vary, so the conjecture\nis genuinely falsifiable by the shape of `X` alone. Under the previous schema\n`⟨0, rfl⟩` closed the class for every choice of everything, including a\none-point scheme, so \"the substrate fluctuates\" had nothing to fail against.\n\nThis is also the precise sense in which the conjecture says more than the\nappendix's existing global `ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.leadingCoeff_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.leadingCoeff_eq","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L152-L156","doc":"**The leading coefficient agrees across points** — part 3 in the form the\nblock states it (\"globally constant\"), rather than pinned to `q₀ − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.standardPart_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.standardPart_const","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L145-L150","doc":"**The archimedean shadow really is constant**, across every pair of points —\nthe sense in which the fluctuation is invisible classically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.standardPart_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.standardPart_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L135-L143","doc":"**The classical substrate is `q = 1` everywhere** — the block's part 2 in\nits own `st` form, derived rather than assumed.\n\nThe class states infinitesimality, which is the block's framing (`ε` is a\nsection of the sheaf of *infinitesimals*); this is the consequence the block\nactually spells out. Uses the corpus's own `standardPart_of_infinitesimal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.leadingCoeff_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.leadingCoeff_const","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L114-L114","doc":"**Part 3.** The leading `ω⁻¹` coefficient is globally constant and equals\nthe archimedean substrate deviation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.local_variation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.local_variation","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L111-L111","doc":"**Part 1 — local variation.** The family is genuinely non-constant.\nWithout this the conjecture collapses to the global `ε` the appendix\nalready has, so a carrier permitting a constant family would assert\nnothing new. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.infinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.infinitesimal","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L106-L106","doc":"**Part 2.** Every local value is infinitesimal, so the classical\nsubstrate is `q = 1` at every point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.LocalInfinitesimalField","kind":"class","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/LocalInfinitesimalField.lean#L84-L114","doc":"**The substrate parameter is a local infinitesimal field.**\n\nThe conjecture of\n[`conj:local-infinitesimal-field`](../../../appendix-surreals/local-infinitesimal-field.md):\n`q(x) = 1 + ε(x)` fluctuates from point to point, every fluctuation is\ninfinitesimal, and the leading surreal coefficient is nevertheless globally\nconstant.\n\nParameters are the caller's data:\n\n* `X` — the index type of points (the block's scheme, taken extensionally;\n  see the header);\n* `ε x` — the local infinitesimal at `x`;\n* `leadingCoeff` — the `ω⁻¹` coefficient in Conway normal form, which this tree\n  does not construct;\n* `q₀` — the archimedean substrate value, a parameter rather than a literal.\n\nAn instance **is** the conjecture, for that data. None is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:local-infinitesimal-field","label":"conj:local-infinitesimal-field","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/local-infinitesimal-field.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}